assistant: `approximateTokens` turns each message into JSON using its own key order, adds up the character counts of those JSON strings, and returns the total divided by four, rounded up. It measures the whole message, not just `content`, so fields like `role`, `toolName`, `toolCallId`, `isError`, `attribution`, `details` and any unknown extra fields all count toward the size. It leaves out keys whose value is `undefined` plus the fields the harness records but never sends to the model: `contextSnapshot`, `usage`, `timestamp`, `api`, `provider`, `model` and `stopReason`.
